  ('94ffb6a4-77dc-5d50-92c0-baec49b24043'::uuid, '7309ff73-dcfd-56d7-81be-d2fa1148d722'::uuid, 'National Health Investors - mortgage, mezzanine and construction loans', 'National Health Investors (NHI) - mortgage, mezzanine and construction loans · Healthcare mezz / pref equity', array['PRIVATE_BRIDGE', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['SENIOR_LIVING', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, 9.0::numeric, 10.0::numeric, 'Directory SL-068: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Mezzanine loans to operators, Construction loans (AL), Mortgage notes (acquisition / refinance) | Rate: 9.0%-10.0% on disclosed 2025 loans (e.g. 9.0% ALF construction loan; 9.4% Vizion Health mezz; 10.0% CFG mezz) | Term: e.g. construction loan maturing April 2030; mezz extended to May 2028 | Broker program: No broker program published. Loans disclosed in SEC filings go to operator relationships (Encore Senior Living construction loan, Vizion Health mezz) and to Capital Funding Group (mezz facility), often alongside purchase options. Treat as a capital source for established operators, not a broker desk. | Fit: REIT that makes loans to operators: up to $28.0M AL construction loan (MI, May 2025), new $18.8M and $11.3M mortgage notes (late 2025), operator mezz. Useful for Corin operator clients who want REIT growth capital; no documented broker channel or CA loan. | Source: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/877860/000087786026000053/nhi-20251231.htm'),
  ('39e16e77-083d-5294-8201-89dd36f57c47'::uuid, '7854c925-f423-54cd-a701-96bcc81db891'::uuid, 'Live Oak Bank', 'Live Oak Bank - Hospitality · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-002: tier A, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504, Conventional hotel acquisition and refinance | Broker program: Pays referral sources an agreed fee on eligible closed, fully funded loans under a standard referral agreement. For SBA loans the referral source and borrower sign Form 159, and the fee is paid no later than 30 days after month-end (per a hosted Live Oak referral document). SBA PLP lender. | Contact: Jamie Bourgeois, Managing Director, Hospitality | Second check: Verified (active 2026: Yes). Live Oak''s own hospitality page lists Jamie Bourgeois as Managing Director, Hospitality (theorg.com still shows her older energy & infrastructure role), and a referral agreement paying fees… | Fit: Other desk of Live Oak Bank (already listed for senior care). Its dedicated hospitality team does SBA and conventional hotel loans nationally and has a documented referral-fee process. Referral fee percentage not published. | Source: https://www.liveoak.bank/commercial/project-finance/real-estate/hospitality/'),
  ('2f2ab5c7-33b9-5c11-879e-d42789a6d134'::uuid, '089cda90-bb1a-5267-a9bf-8cebd715592c'::uuid, 'Basis Multifamily Finance', 'Basis Multifamily Finance · Agency multifamily (Fannie / Freddie)', array['AGENCY']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], 'non_recourse'::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-001: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Fannie Mae DUS (conventional; Fannie small loans available to DUS lenders) | Recourse: Non-recourse w/ carve-outs (Fannie Mae DUS standard) | Broker program: Not documented in searches. | Fit: Newest independent Fannie DUS lender before 2026 and the only African American- and women-owned (MWBE) DUS lender; parent Basis Investment Group also runs a national CRE credit platform. California lending and broker policy unconfirmed. | Source: https://fanniemae.com/newsroom/fannie-mae-news/basis-multifamily-finance-network-dus-lenders'),
  ('84320db4-5d7b-53c2-bcba-c2c71ae52f22'::uuid, '3a4a0721-eee6-5821-9e88-6cd20b0735f0'::uuid, 'Citi Community Capital', 'Citi Community Capital · Agency multifamily (Fannie / Freddie)', array['HUD_MULTIFAMILY', 'AGENCY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], 'non_recourse'::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-002: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National; active California LIHTC lender (Los Angeles underwriting team) | Programs (as published): Freddie Mac Optigo Targeted Affordable Housing (acquisition, refinance, moderate rehab), Fannie Mae DUS (fixed and ARM), FHA MAP (non-recourse construction), Tax-exempt bond / LIHTC construction and permanent loans | Recourse: Non-recourse (FHA construction loans) | Broker program: Not documented. Citi lends directly; no correspondent or broker program found. | Fit: Ranked #1 affordable housing lender for 16 straight years ($7.0B in 2024) and sells California LIHTC loan pools via CMFA. Best for large affordable / tax-credit deals; not a small-broker shop. | Source: https://www.citigroup.com/icg/sa/citicommunitycapital/'),
  ('bf8b5755-cfb7-5e89-9021-decc8d6958b0'::uuid, 'd5279a03-e5dd-555c-b6cf-1d341575d199'::uuid, 'Fifth Third Bank - Fannie Mae DUS Multifamily', 'Fifth Third Bank - Fannie Mae DUS Multifamily (former Mechanics Bank DUS team) · Agency multifamily (Fannie / Freddie)', array['AGENCY']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], 'non_recourse'::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-003: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (DUS); team inherited from Walnut Creek, CA-based Mechanics Bank | Programs (as published): Fannie Mae DUS (conventional and small loans) | Recourse: Non-recourse w/ carve-outs (Fannie Mae DUS standard) | Broker program: Not documented yet. Fifth Third bought the ~$1.8B DUS servicing portfolio for about $126M cash and hired the Mechanics employees who run the business; no broker / correspondent policy published. | Fit: Status changed in 2026: Mechanics Bank (excluded earlier) sold its DUS line to Fifth Third (Fifth Third Healthcare was excluded earlier; this is a different desk). The new DUS team came out of a California bank and is building volume, so it may welcome broker… | Source: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260507725218/en/'),
  ('e397f019-bc04-5690-98dc-82a489637418'::uuid, '3d4cd7a7-2c7a-52d3-af9a-17910d61c355'::uuid, 'Pinnacle Real Estate Capital Markets - Small Balance Lending', 'Pinnacle Real Estate Capital Markets - Small Balance Lending · Agency multifamily (Fannie / Freddie)', array['AGENCY']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, 1000000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], 'non_recourse'::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-004: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (originators work nationwide); SBL office in Dallas | Programs (as published): Freddie Mac Optigo Conventional Small (replaced legacy Optigo SBL on 2026-04-15), legacy Freddie Mac SBL (hybrid ARM, fixed, interest-only options) | Recourse: Non-recourse (Freddie Mac small balance structure) | Broker program: Lender page says its originators ''develop relationships with commercial mortgage bankers, brokers and financial institutions nationwide''. Pinnacle was one of about 11 seller/servicers authorized for Freddie SBL and was selected as a seller/servicer for the new Conventional Small program. | Contact: Jim Going, SVP, Head of Multifamily SBL team | Second check: Corrected (active 2026: Yes). Pinnacle survived its Synovus merger (closed Jan 1, 2026; holding company now in Atlanta, bank in Nashville), and Jim Going is confirmed as head of the agency SBL team now in Freddie''s Opti… | Fit: One of only ~10-11 Freddie small-balance seller/servicers and openly works with brokers; good outlet for 5-50 unit California apartments at agency pricing (loans under $10M). If the 2025 Pinnacle-Synovus merger closes (not verified in this round), this desk i… | Source: https://recm.pnfp.com/small-balance-lending/'),
  ('9dfa559a-124f-58e3-aa4a-60d4613c93e0'::uuid, 'ab692ef2-88a6-5795-97bf-a3f7be81ec05'::uuid, 'R4 Capital Funding', 'R4 Capital Funding (R4CF) · Agency multifamily (Fannie / Freddie)', array['AGENCY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-005: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (31 states + DC financed); R4 runs California LIHTC equity funds | Programs (as published): Tax-exempt mortgage revenue bond construction and permanent loans (direct purchase / securitized), paired with R4 LIHTC equity | Broker program: Not documented. | Fit: Not a Fannie / Freddie lender; filed under agency as the closest bucket for affordable permanent debt (an alternative to Freddie TAH bond executions). R4CF provided $925M of construction and perm debt in 2025 (4,398 units, +34%), and R4''s 2025 California fund… | Source: https://www.housingfinance.com/finance/r4-capital-reports-21-billion-affordable-housing-investments-2025'),
