  ('9749768b-b09d-5516-8f96-87edc254840f'::uuid, '1bbd752a-9b10-5fed-a852-b866d9d30ba6'::uuid, 'Highland Commercial Mortgage', 'Highland Commercial Mortgage · HUD multifamily (221(d)(4) / 223(f))', array['HUD_MULTIFAMILY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['SENIOR_LIVING', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], 'non_recourse'::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-011: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Programs (as published): HUD 221(d)(4) new construction, FHA multifamily, Affordable housing, Senior living / healthcare FHA loans | Term: Long-term, fully amortizing, fixed rate (HUD 221(d)(4)) | Recourse: Non-recourse (HUD 221(d)(4)) | Broker program: None published. | Fit: Active FHA MAP lender: in June 2026 it announced HUD 221(d)(4) financing for a 270-unit Class A community in Orlando (president Chip Moore). Deals found are in the Southeast; broker channel and California lending unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.einpresswire.com/article/921885181?promo=4400'),
  ('06aa6f6f-ce26-52ef-989a-84343ee46c52'::uuid, 'bd2e1563-815c-5f12-a670-8bdd8679f79d'::uuid, 'The Bancorp Bank - Real Estate Bridge Lending', 'The Bancorp Bank - Real Estate Bridge Lending (REBL) · Multifamily bridge / value-add', array['PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], 200000000::bigint, 6000000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-012: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (value-add multifamily nationwide; book concentrated in Sun Belt) | Programs (as published): Value-add multifamily bridge (acquisition + capex), balance-sheet funded | Leverage: Up to 80% of purchase price + 100% of capital improvement budget | Term: 3-yr initial + two 1-yr extensions | Broker program: Not documented. Product page targets investors in value-add multifamily nationwide; no broker page found. | Fit: $2.2B apartment bridge book funded on a bank balance sheet (no warehouse line), $2M-$60M+. California activity and broker acceptance unconfirmed; a 2025 class action concerns its Sun Belt syndicator loans. | Source: https://thebancorp.com/solution/real-estate-bridge-lending'),
  ('55ce1cc3-b94c-53f1-8371-60608a6cf94f'::uuid, 'e7b2cbfe-20c6-576a-8e80-8747028623d7'::uuid, 'Veleta Capital Partners', 'Veleta Capital Partners (VCP) · Multifamily bridge / value-add', array['PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['SENIOR_LIVING', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, 2000000000::bigint, null::numeric, 68.0::numeric, array['first']::text[], 'non_recourse'::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-013: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National, focus on Western U.S. and Sunbelt | Programs (as published): Senior secured transitional / bridge loans (floating and fixed), renovation and ADU-conversion bridge | Leverage: 68% LTC on a cited Dallas deal | Term: 12-36 months | Recourse: Non-recourse (cited Dallas deal) | Broker program: No published broker program, but 2023 deals were announced as brokered by outside intermediaries (Bellwether Enterprise arranged a Dallas loan). Press contact press@veletacapital.com per the TriPost release. | Email: press@veletacapital.com | Second check: Flagged (active 2026: Unclear). The latest news is the May 2025 TriPost investment anchoring Veleta Fund II, the newest CA loan found is the Jan 2023 Northridge bridge loan, and no broker program or broker-arranged 2024… | Fit: Los Angeles-based small-balance apartment bridge platform (loans up to $20M) with California deals such as a $12.6M Northridge 42-unit renovation; takes intermediary-arranged deals. Confirm broker fee policy directly. | Source: https://theregistrysocal.com/veleta-capital-partners-secures-12-6mm-bridge-loan-for-42-unit-multifamily-project-in-northridge/'),
  ('7f000ef0-e04b-50ac-ba27-34c188857090'::uuid, '6e2ed7db-c0d9-573e-a277-efb50e318804'::uuid, 'Leste Group', 'Leste Group (Leste Real Estate Credit) · Multifamily bridge / value-add', array['PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-015: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Multifamily loans (refinance / transitional), Preferred equity, Real estate credit | Broker program: Not documented. Trade press says Leste aims to grow multifamily originations from about $125M in 2025 to $1B a year; deals listed on Traded (e.g. $29.1M refinance loan on a 287-unit St. Louis property). | Fit: Growing multifamily credit platform (2025-2026) that also does preferred equity; past San Diego office credit investment, but no California multifamily loan found and no broker program published. | Source: https://www.multihousingnews.com/the-leste-groups-great-american-story/'),
  ('b203ae21-a68e-5f92-a7e4-486b7bcbbf1c'::uuid, 'b4779422-6e27-53f3-a9fa-d89a8b9c4f1c'::uuid, 'Pembrook Capital Management', 'Pembrook Capital Management · Multifamily bridge / value-add', array['PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-016: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (deals in IL, OH, NY and others) | Programs (as published): First-mortgage bridge loans (acquisition / renovation / recapitalization), Mezzanine loans, Secured lines of credit | Broker program: Not documented. | Fit: Specialist bridge lender for affordable / workforce apartments (~148 investments approaching $2B and 15,000+ units by May 2024; e.g. $28.2M Ohio recap, $20.3M Chicago portfolio). Useful for LIHTC / workforce value-add, but no California deal or broker program… | Source: https://nyrej.com/pembrook-nears-2-billion-in-affordable-workforce-housing-loan-volume'),
  ('8bca50cb-ad4f-551d-ab2e-ee6080ac34ab'::uuid, 'e6231754-ddd6-5e91-b440-4f6c3380f3ba'::uuid, 'ClearEdge Lending', 'ClearEdge Lending · Small-balance multifamily (5-50 units)', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, 200000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-018: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Programs (as published): DSCR 5-8 unit / 2-8 unit mixed-use investor loans (wholesale) | Broker program: Wholesale lender: its site has a broker ''Price Your Loan'' pricing page listing a ''5-8 Units/2-8 Mixed Use'' DSCR product, and a March 2024 broker flyer for the 5-8 unit program (loans up to $2M, reserves as low as 9 months, experienced investors). | Broker page: https://clearedgelending.com/?p=9998670 | Fit: Wholesale channel for very small apartment buildings (5-8 units) that agency and bank lenders often skip. The flyer is from March 2024 and California eligibility is unconfirmed, so get the current matrix from an account executive. | Source: https://clearedgelending.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/REA-5-8-Units-3.4.24.pdf'),
  ('d9a93f6b-42d9-5c5b-aa56-c66d7a4295f8'::uuid, '209c7d47-5645-5ec5-b9da-a5a7a140b1b8'::uuid, 'theLender', 'theLender (Hometown Equity Mortgage, LLC) · Small-balance multifamily (5-50 units)', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-019: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Multi-state; California-based | Programs (as published): NONI58 DSCR (5-8 unit residential and 2-8 unit mixed-use), NearNONI DSCR, Blanket portfolio DSCR, Foreign National DSCR, Cash-out refinance | Broker program: Runs a wholesale (broker) channel at wholesale.thelender.com that publishes a ''NONI58'' matrix for 5-8 residential units and 2-8 unit mixed-use (versions dated 2024-06-01, 2025-12 and 2026-03-23): minimum DSCR 1.00, 75% purchase LTV at 700 FICO, commercial space limited to retail, office or restaurant. Says it has funded over $3B of DSCR loans since 2019. | Broker page: https://wholesale.thelender.com | Fit: California wholesale DSCR lender with a current (March 2026) 5-8 unit matrix; useful for very small apartment buildings that agency and bank lenders will not do. Covers only 5-8 units, not larger small-balance deals. | Source: https://wholesale.thelender.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/NONI58_03.23.26.pdf'),
  ('1eea9a7d-7a24-57b5-adb2-027b81d4ac38'::uuid, '8b771b64-9c26-5a9b-89ae-d33bb16f8044'::uuid, 'Forward Lending', 'Forward Lending · Small-balance multifamily (5-50 units)', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, 300000000::bigint, 75.0::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-020: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Programs (as published): DSCR 5-8 unit (interest-only available), DSCR Fusion, DSCR Foreign National, Non-QM DSCR / no-ratio | Leverage: 75% LTV (720+ FICO purchase / rate-term); 65% cash-out | Broker program: Wholesale (broker) lender: publishes broker-facing 5-8 unit matrices (Oct 2024, Jul 2025, May 2026, Aug 2026) and monthly broker webinars (latest July 2026: ''DSCR 5-8 up to $3M loan amount / 75% Max LTV / IO available''). Minimum FICO 680, minimum DSCR 1.00; experienced investors only; LLC / partnership / corporate vesting allowed; mixed-use not eligible (2024 guide). | Phone: 844-941-5626 | Fit: Current (2026) wholesale DSCR program for 5-8 unit buildings up to $3M. Its 5-8 unit terms and webinar titles match LendingPros'' materials, so the two may be affiliated brands; check before opening both accounts. HQ and California licensing not confirmed. | Source: https://forwardlendingmtg.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Forward-Lending-Broker-Webinar-July-2026-DSCR-Fusion-and-DSCR-5_8.pdf'),
  ('280c8b04-b9d3-522a-bb85-c25b95669f59'::uuid, '9381c113-4f49-5e86-b811-b6727fb461fe'::uuid, 'HomeXpress Mortgage Corp.', 'HomeXpress Mortgage Corp. (HomeX) · Small-balance multifamily (5-50 units)', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, 75.0::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-021: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: 28 states (wholesale partners) | Programs (as published): InvestorX DSCR 5-8 units (business-purpose), CoreX and other non-QM wholesale programs | Leverage: 75% LTV purchase at 720+ FICO; 70% at 680-700 (2023 InvestorX 5-8 rate sheet) | Broker program: Wholesale non-QM lender licensed to work with mortgage brokers and mortgage bankers in 28 states; broker-access page, products and pricing in the ARIVE LOS, and an InvestorX 5-8 unit rate sheet marked ''for wholesale and loan broker use only'' (2023). | Broker page: https://homexmortgage.com/broker-access | Fit: Wholesale lender with a 5-8 unit DSCR product; useful for very small apartment buildings. Rate sheets found are from 2023 and California is not confirmed among its 28 states. | Source: https://homexmortgage.com/broker-access'),
  ('4a629c92-4dad-5a3a-8635-9321522efefa'::uuid, '5d870545-cd12-50d1-b87d-b5c6a21adf03'::uuid, 'LendingPros', 'LendingPros · Small-balance multifamily (5-50 units)', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, 300000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-022: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Programs (as published): DSCR 5-8 unit, Non-QM DSCR | Broker program: Wholesale lender that runs broker webinars (Oct 2024 ''DSCR 5-8 Unit'' broker webinar) and publishes broker / AE non-QM overviews (July, Aug, Dec 2025; June 2026). The June 2026 overview lists DSCR 5-8 units to $3M, minimum FICO 680, minimum DSCR 1.00. | Fit: Wholesale channel with a current 5-8 unit DSCR product up to $3M. Narrow (5-8 units only), and HQ / California licensing not confirmed. Program terms and webinar titles match Forward Lending''s, so the two may be affiliated brands. | Source: https://golendingpros.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/LendingPros-AE-NonQMOverview-060826.pdf'),
  ('d05391ad-6bd3-512e-8fca-fc330af921d5'::uuid, '0580b2ae-ec7d-5b0e-a1cd-d5ee5d618f9a'::uuid, 'Lendz Financial', 'Lendz Financial · Small-balance multifamily (5-50 units)', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, 75.0::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-023: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Programs (as published): DSCR 5-8 units, DSCR 2-8 unit mixed-use (non-QM) | Leverage: 75% LTV (DSCR 5-8) | Broker program: Wholesale-only platform with an online submission page (lendzfinancial.com/submit) and broker-education content. DSCR 5-8: minimum 700 FICO, up to 75% LTV, minimum DSCR 1.00, all units leased; loans of $2M+ also need debt yield of 9% or more. | Broker page: https://lendzfinancial.com/submit | Fit: Wholesale non-QM lender with a published 5-8 unit and 2-8 unit mixed-use DSCR product for brokers. HQ, state licensing and California lending not confirmed in searches. | Source: https://www.lendzfinancial.com/program/dscr-loans-5-8-units-2-8-mixed-use'),
  ('cbd75d9f-e60d-52ac-9a66-1c4c46d68413'::uuid, '256b6386-d5ea-5906-ae8b-e76dd8eb572a'::uuid, 'California Community Reinvestment Corporation', 'California Community Reinvestment Corporation (CCRC) · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-024: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California only | Programs (as published): Permanent loans for acquisition / rehab of affordable apartments, Forward commitments for new construction, Direct purchase of tax-exempt bonds, Taxable mortgage pool loans | Broker program: Not documented. | Fit: California-only CDFI permanent lender for affordable apartments, from small loans (e.g. $1.33M San Diego perm in 2026) up; added more than $120M of lending capacity in 2026 through a $114M securitization and more bank capital. Good for rent-restricted deals;… | Source: https://www.housingfinance.com/finance/california-community-reinvestment-corp-boosts-lending-capacity-affordable-housing'),
  ('26e9389a-4642-500e-bd43-66b33a4d9633'::uuid, '93478a0f-73fe-51e4-9b8a-f837a656f40d'::uuid, 'Citizens Business Bank', 'Citizens Business Bank · Community bank / credit union CRE', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory BK-006: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California statewide (all major metros after the Heritage merger added 16 Bay Area branches) | Programs (as published): CRE loans, Owner-occupied CRE, SBA (Heritage SBA PLP team) | Broker program: No broker program found. It is a relationship bank. | Fit: California''s largest community-bank platform (about $21B in assets), statewide after the Heritage merger. Strong CRE capacity, but it is a relationship lender and broker acceptance is unconfirmed. | Source: https://investors.cbbank.com/node/17056/pdf'),
  ('02bc5f34-7c89-5dbb-98f6-012b3319d23d'::uuid, '93478a0f-73fe-51e4-9b8a-f837a656f40d'::uuid, 'Citizens Business Bank', 'Citizens Business Bank · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-025: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California | Programs (as published): Portfolio multifamily loans (balances reported in call reports); no published product terms | Broker program: None found. One search returned only call-report data; most results were for the unrelated Citizens Bank (Citizens Financial Group). | Fit: California bank with about $836.4M of multifamily loans on its call report. Product terms and broker policy were not found, so treat as a relationship-bank lead. | Source: https://visbanking.com/call-report/citizens-business-bank-national-association-reports-933966/loans/multifamily'),
  ('0226ed70-19b4-573c-a09a-182482ec60ad'::uuid, '25e24f87-1537-58df-afab-b6186a4c097d'::uuid, 'City First Bank, N.A.', 'City First Bank, N.A. · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-026: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Los Angeles and Washington, DC regions (CDFI) | Programs (as published): Multifamily portfolio loans (mostly adjustable-rate), Affordable housing preservation loans | Broker program: Not documented. | Fit: Mission-driven CDFI bank whose book is about 58% multifamily ($593M at 2025 year-end), rooted in Los Angeles through Broadway Federal. Fits workforce / affordable apartment deals in LMI areas; broker acceptance unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.cityfirstbank.com/?p=978'),
  ('b3c4c05f-ae26-51d5-a62e-300c0d00f8c2'::uuid, '14c260c3-7b72-50a4-aa2c-68f61e0cac9d'::uuid, 'Farmers & Merchants Bank of Long Beach', 'Farmers & Merchants Bank of Long Beach · Community bank / credit union CRE', array['BANK_LIFE_CO', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory BK-009: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Southern California (Los Angeles, Orange County, Inland Empire) | Programs (as published): CRE loans, Construction loans, Multifamily loans, Commercial business loans | Broker program: No broker program found. | Fit: A very well-capitalized Southern California bank that has historically been a heavy real estate lender, including multifamily. Brokered-deal acceptance and terms are unconfirmed, and most of the sources are third-party. | Source: https://altss.com/profile/farmers-and-merchants-bank'),
  ('518660d2-97f9-53ba-944c-a2a14b27ba70'::uuid, '14c260c3-7b72-50a4-aa2c-68f61e0cac9d'::uuid, 'Farmers & Merchants Bank of Long Beach', 'Farmers & Merchants Bank of Long Beach · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-027: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California state-chartered bank headquartered in Long Beach | Programs (as published): Portfolio multifamily residential loans (balances reported in its call reports); no published product terms | Broker program: None found. No multifamily product page, broker page or referral program surfaced in searches (wave 1 also found none). Approach through the bank''s commercial real estate lending team. | Fit: Long Beach bank with a multifamily residential loan book tracked in its call reports (RC-C data at 12/31/2025). Useful for Southern California apartment deals, but no product terms or broker channel are published. | Source: https://visbanking.com/call-report/farmers-and-merchants-bank-of-long-beach-reports-871769/loans/multifamily'),
  ('420f9bf6-ce36-5eae-94c1-0cc2d843ef2d'::uuid, 'bf09e2ce-663a-5ede-9d75-ee7881bbe599'::uuid, 'JPMorgan Chase - Commercial Term Lending', 'JPMorgan Chase - Commercial Term Lending (Multifamily) · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], 50000000::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-028: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National; California teams in Los Angeles, Orange County, Sacramento, San Diego, San Francisco | Programs (as published): Stabilized multifamily term loans (Commercial Term Lending) | Broker program: Not documented. Chase pages describe a direct, streamlined process (LOI on two years of operating history and a recent rent roll; tax returns not required; costs the greater of $2,000 or 12.5 bps of the loan). No broker or referral program found. | Broker page: https://www.chase.com/mfl | Contact: Jake Bade, Managing Director, California Multifamily Lending | Fit: Largest bank apartment lender in California with low closing costs ($500K to over $25M). Brokers can introduce clients, but Chase publishes no broker compensation program, so fee must come from the borrower. | Source: https://www.jpmorgan.com/commercial-real-estate/multifamily-property-loans'),
  ('6ddaaada-e9ed-5944-b91a-5de8f3d3cf3b'::uuid, '072d2cb5-8774-5cea-bf05-0f74037ee3f0'::uuid, 'Logix Federal Credit Union', 'Logix Federal Credit Union · Community bank / credit union CRE', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory BK-012: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Southern California (Santa Clarita Valley / Los Angeles area); also buys CRE participations | Programs (as published): CRE purchase and refinance, Adjustable-rate CRE term loans (fixed for at least 5 years, 5% lifetime cap), CRE loan participations, SBA | Leverage: Up to 70% financing on new CRE purchases | Broker program: No broker program found. It actively buys CRE loan participations from other credit unions. | Fit: An LA-area credit union with a real CRE program and a published 70% LTV, including multifamily. Lender type is set to ''Bank'' (no credit-union value). Broker acceptance is unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.logixbanking.com/business/commercial-real-estate'),
  ('ce0189ef-5be5-59a8-989c-930983b79db5'::uuid, '072d2cb5-8774-5cea-bf05-0f74037ee3f0'::uuid, 'Logix Federal Credit Union', 'Logix Federal Credit Union - Commercial Real Estate · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-029: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Southern California credit union (Valencia HQ); also sells CRE loan participations to other credit unions | Programs (as published): Commercial real estate term loans (purchase and refinance), CRE loan participations sold to credit unions | Leverage: Up to 70% on a new purchase | Broker program: No broker program found on its business lending pages. Credit union lending may require membership; ask the commercial lending team. | Fit: SoCal credit union whose CRE page lists multifamily and advertises up to 70% purchase financing. Job postings show an active multifamily underwriting team. Broker acceptance is unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.logixbanking.com/business/commercial-real-estate'),
  ('8814b855-7902-547d-9901-0b3fc89ee3a5'::uuid, '3d29861e-a8de-5a07-880b-7a568d6e9fc4'::uuid, 'Malaga Bank', 'Malaga Bank · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-030: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Southern / Central Coast California (Santa Barbara to San Diego) | Programs (as published): Multifamily portfolio loans (purchase, refinance), 1-4 unit investor loans incl. construction, Commercial investment property loans | Broker program: Not documented. Malaga''s lending page lists named income-property lending officers and says it is a portfolio lender that does not sell its loans (local decisions). No broker program found; ask the income property team whether it accepts broker submissions. | Phone: 310-544-7800 | Fit: SoCal apartment-focused portfolio lender (multifamily concentration is its core business). Broker acceptance unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.malagabank.com/lending'),
  ('eaef5dd0-be16-561c-afc6-6edbb0c3a76d'::uuid, '167c40e5-3801-5927-a541-825542c8acdc'::uuid, 'Poppy Bank', 'Poppy Bank · Community bank / credit union CRE', array['BANK_LIFE_CO', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['SENIOR_LIVING', 'COMMERCIAL', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory BK-013: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California (Bay Area, Sacramento, Southern California branches); LPOs in UT, TX, NY, SC | Programs (as published): CRE loans, Construction loans, SBA 7(a), SBA 504, USDA loans, Commercial loans and lines | Broker program: No broker program found. The bank says it responds quickly and turns applications around fast. | Phone: 888-636-9994 | Fit: A fast-growing California business bank (about $6-7B in assets, 17th largest in CA) that does CRE, construction and SBA/USDA loans. Commercial Observer reports a $43M Southern California senior-housing loan, which is relevant to Corin''s healthcare book. | Source: https://poppy.bank/about-us'),
  ('b4b1c040-92a9-5887-b562-211d0c277401'::uuid, '167c40e5-3801-5927-a541-825542c8acdc'::uuid, 'Poppy Bank', 'Poppy Bank · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO', 'PRIVATE_BRIDGE', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['SENIOR_LIVING', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-031: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California (branches listed in Walnut Creek, Fremont, Los Altos, Costa Mesa and Beverly Hills chamber directories) | Programs (as published): Commercial real estate, Construction, SBA / USDA loans, Multifamily portfolio loans, Healthcare (SNF) bridge loans | Broker program: No broker page found. Evidence it takes intermediary-arranged deals: Berkadia announced in June 2024 that it worked with Poppy Bank to close 12 SNF bridge loans totaling over $329.7M. That evidence is healthcare, not apartments. | Fit: California community bank with about $728.5M of multifamily residential loans at year-end 2025 (call report). It has closed broker-arranged healthcare bridge loans, so ask whether its CRE team takes broker multifamily submissions. | Source: https://poppy.bank/about-us'),
  ('8b6e9d39-0a0c-5e5d-ad08-d1b2638fe653'::uuid, 'a4c0f713-2b2c-54e5-9ce5-af6ac1a805c8'::uuid, 'Provident Savings Bank', 'Provident Savings Bank (Provident Bank Mortgage) · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], 50000000::bigint, null::bigint, 75.0::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-032: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California (Inland Empire / Southern California focus) | Programs (as published): Commercial / multifamily 5+ unit portfolio loans (wholesale rate sheet) | Leverage: 75% LTV (multifamily, per April 2025 rate sheet) | Broker program: Provident Bank Mortgage runs a wholesale channel (pbmwholesale.com). A Provident loan-officer presentation points brokers to a wholesale rate sheet for ''Commercial / Multi-Family 5+ Units'', and a Provident Riverside rate sheet dated 2025-04-18 lists multifamily programs up to 75% LTV with a $500,000 minimum on the ''A'' program. | Second check: Corrected (active 2026: Yes). The FY2026 10-K (June 30, 2026) confirms it is active and lends in Southern and Northern California, with multifamily about 40% of loans, but no broker or referral program for multifamily w… | Fit: California savings bank with a wholesale (broker) channel that publishes a 5+ unit multifamily rate sheet; good for small-balance Inland Empire / SoCal apartment deals. Rate sheet is April 2025, so confirm current terms. | Source: https://www.myprovident.com/agent/rates_Gkoenen.pdf'),
  ('00a506d4-f463-580c-84d5-dcf4d2dc3e36'::uuid, '0953dcdc-5486-52ca-bf1b-4b7f679d20e4'::uuid, 'Self-Help Federal Credit Union - Multifamily Housing Loans', 'Self-Help Federal Credit Union - Multifamily Housing Loans · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['SENIOR_LIVING', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], 50000000::bigint, 2000000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-033: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California, Illinois, Washington, Wisconsin (FCU branches); California commercial lending growth push | Programs (as published): Construction-to-permanent senior debt, Permanent senior debt for preservation or creation of affordable multifamily | Broker program: Not documented. Self-Help job posting says it is growing California commercial lending (typically $500K-$20M) incl. affordable housing and CRE; borrowers may be individuals, partnerships, LLCs, corporations, nonprofits or for-profits. | Fit: CDFI credit union with a stated 5-75 unit multifamily focus for affordable / workforce rentals and an active California expansion; good for mission-aligned small apartment deals. Broker acceptance unconfirmed; $500K-$20M range is from a job ad, not a term she… | Source: https://www.self-helpfcu.org/business/loans/commercial-loans/multifamily-housing-loans'),
  ('9ee70ddd-ca97-5f65-a7ed-26bdbbec1b45'::uuid, '896d4281-f4fa-54ef-898a-f669741e1a41'::uuid, 'Bay Federal Credit Union', 'Bay Federal Credit Union · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-034: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California only (only California commercial properties are eligible) | Programs (as published): Commercial real estate loans incl. 5+ unit multifamily | Broker program: Not documented. | Fit: California-only credit union CRE program that includes 5+ unit multifamily; broker channel unconfirmed, so treat as a relationship call. | Source: https://bayfed.com/business/commercial-real-estate'),
  ('359f2035-9053-520b-9926-baf1ef2faf20'::uuid, '5707c92c-de27-5881-bd1c-d1c4d7ac1a80'::uuid, 'Orange County''s Credit Union', 'Orange County''s Credit Union · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-035: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Southern California | Programs (as published): Multifamily investment property loans (5+ units), Commercial real estate loans | Broker program: Not documented. CRE page lists a senior commercial real estate loan officer as the contact; no broker program found. | Fit: CDFI credit union that lends on 5+ unit apartment buildings in Southern California; a possible outlet for small local deals, but broker acceptance and compensation are unconfirmed. | Source: https://orangecountyscu.org/products/business-services/commercial-real-estate-lending'),
  ('ca128812-11ed-5de5-ab9a-9f552b14ebb2'::uuid, '9c304ec4-04e0-564f-8dd0-02c27d7e1d7c'::uuid, 'WaFd Bank', 'WaFd Bank (Washington Federal) · Multifamily bank / credit union', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory MF-036: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Western U.S. incl. former Luther Burbank California branches | Programs (as published): Multifamily and CRE portfolio loans (legacy Luther Burbank income-property lending) | Broker program: Not confirmed for 2026. Luther Burbank historically worked with independent mortgage brokers (wholesale). After the merger WaFd sold $2.8B of the acquired multifamily loans (2024); no current WaFd broker program for California multifamily was found. | Fit: Successor to Luther Burbank, once a top-25 U.S. multifamily lender based in California. WaFd shrank the acquired apartment book in 2024, so appetite and broker acceptance need a call. | Source: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20241017054297/en/WaFd-Inc.-Announces-Fourth-Quarter-and-Fiscal-2024-Results/'),
  ('0b94277d-40db-539d-b8d7-e6521ca0119c'::uuid, '943048ab-45bb-5a1d-9c66-ab55719ddbc6'::uuid, 'Celtic Bank', 'Celtic Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-001: tier A, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (business development officers nationwide) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504 / CDC, USDA B&I, SBA CAPLines ($500k-$5M) | Broker program: Has a documented referral partner program: Celtic ''works with loan brokers, business consultants, and relationship managers'' and ''offers referral fees to qualified partners'', with a dedicated business development officer for each partner. Approved partners can send deals right away. SBA PLP lender. | Broker page: https://celticbank.com/referral-form | Second check: Verified (active 2026: Yes). The referral-partner application and partner page (referral fees, broker portal, dedicated BDO) are on celticbank.com, the bank was active in 2026 (FY2026 7(a) volume, April 2026 Casca deal)… | Fit: A national SBA PLP lender with a published broker channel and over 20 years of hotel acquisition and construction lending (per NerdWallet/Biz2Credit). Hotel-specific terms not published. | Source: https://www.celticbank.com/partner'),
  ('d6100853-8ea6-5da6-9763-4d8597fe3d74'::uuid, '7e27df13-67e3-5171-a70f-4487380490fd'::uuid, 'American Plus Bank', 'American Plus Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-003: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: San Gabriel Valley, CA community bank | Programs (as published): CRE purchase and refinance loans, SBA loans (real estate, equipment, refinance, tenant improvements) | Broker program: None published. | Fit: Arcadia community bank whose commercial loan page names hotels/motels among CRE purchase and refinance collateral, and which also offers SBA loans. A third-party aggregator puts recorded mortgage volume at about $98.8M over 12 months (average $2.3M). Hotel-SB… | Source: https://bankaplus.com/Commercial-Loans.aspx'),
  ('4b4bac34-b005-508d-8c9d-a473a2902ba7'::uuid, '3178e5e2-a8a1-585e-9c13-85740ffd7f9d'::uuid, 'Bank of Hope', 'Bank of Hope · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-004: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National Korean-American bank; SBA 7(a) loans funded in all states (per PeerSense) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504, SBA Express (to $350k), Export Working Capital, EZ loans (non-SBA) | Broker program: No published broker program found. Its SBA page lists 7(a), 504, Export Working Capital and Express. The Korea Herald ranked it #6 among Korean-American SBA lenders (FY2026). Ask the SBA desk about Form 159 referral fees for hotel deals. | Fit: The largest Korean-American bank in the US and a major SBA 7(a)/504 lender headquartered in LA. Hotel-specific program not published, and no broker channel documented. | Source: https://www.bankofhope.com:443/business-lending/sba-lending'),
  ('d7fb9ee2-206e-53b8-8f8e-2e3be284bd93'::uuid, 'ff26095f-4120-5976-a9be-efbe52995c69'::uuid, 'CBB Bank', 'CBB Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-006: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: CA-based; 10 branches, 3 regional SBA offices, 5 loan production offices | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), Commercial real estate | Broker program: No published broker program found. An SBA data tracker shows 980 SBA 7(a) approvals totaling $1.25B from FY2020 to Q1 FY2026. Ask the SBA regional offices about Form 159 referral fees. | Fit: CBB Bank and Commonwealth Business Bank are the same bank, so it has one record here. A high-volume Korean-American SBA 7(a) lender in LA. Hotel share not confirmed in sources found. | Source: https://ir.cbb-bank.com'),
  ('237f2e45-9cf2-58fe-a80e-496e9851dbda'::uuid, '21a5916c-da7d-5b1d-b1a3-b73f19997c9a'::uuid, 'Enterprise Bank & Trust - SBA Lending', 'Enterprise Bank & Trust - SBA Lending · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-007: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Multi-state bank; SBA operations in San Diego, CA (former Seacoast Commerce team) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504, SBA construction loans | Broker program: No broker or referral program found. Its SBA team is in San Diego (SBA servicing, construction processor and business development roles posted there). | Fit: Surviving brand of Seacoast Commerce Bank (excluded in wave 1 as acquired). Its site has a hotel case study (Shree Hospitality) where it used an SBA 504 loan. Caveat: in October 2025 it disclosed seven Southern California CRE loans totaling $68.4M in foreclos… | Source: https://www.enterprisebank.com/insights/loan-options-guidance-entrepreneur-grow-shree-hospitality-llc'),
  ('81519379-dde2-5941-a671-fefe6eca2032'::uuid, '8d2970e4-b4ca-58fb-be3f-07138f1d49f3'::uuid, 'First General Bank', 'First General Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-008: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: SoCal-based; SBA loans in 8 states (per PeerSense) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (PLP), Interim construction loans, CRE, Trade finance | Broker program: No published broker program found. PeerSense lists it as SBA PLP, with its highest SBA franchise volume in Motel 6, Quality Inn and Best Western. The FDIC CRA report notes interim construction lending and a loan book that is about 97% real estate. | Fit: A Chinese-American SGV bank (about $1.1B in assets) doing SBA 7(a) and construction loans for franchised economy hotels. Fits CA motel/hotel 7(a) and small hotel construction. Broker channel unconfirmed. | Source: https://crapes.fdic.gov/publish/2023/58060_231204.PDF'),
  ('f7dace9b-e82f-53a7-8041-427ac2b20b86'::uuid, 'f746fb3d-3bad-5dfc-903f-bdb2225227d7'::uuid, 'First Internet Bank - SBA Lending', 'First Internet Bank - SBA Lending · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-009: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National SBA team (all industries nationwide) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (Preferred Lender) | Broker program: Its SBA origination runs on referral partners and brokers. Press releases describe BDOs who serve ''clients and referral partners'', one with ties to business and real estate brokers. A job posting says associates source deals ''through a network of referral sources and brokers''. The bank calls itself a top-10 SBA 7(a) lender (2023). Fee terms not published. | Fit: A national SBA PLP lender built around a broker channel, which suits 7(a) hotel franchise acquisitions. Hotel appetite not documented, so ask before sending motel or hotel files. | Source: https://www.firstib.com/press-and-news/first-internet-bank-adds-to-sba-team-welcomes-new-senior-business-development-officer/'),
  ('08d094fd-9993-5c55-a0f7-3092079d1891'::uuid, '55b1c05a-63be-57f0-9a68-6ba1033b4925'::uuid, 'GBank', 'GBank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, 72.0::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-010: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National SBA lending in 42 states (per 2026 investor presentation) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), USDA B&I | Leverage: Hotel portfolio weighted LTV 72% (6/30/2026) | Broker program: No published broker program found. GBank says it is the leading originator of hotel SBA loans in the US (#1 hotel SBA lender per SBALenders.com, March 2023) and originated over $550M of 7(a) loans in 2025. GoSBA ranks it #1 for 2025 hotel/motel SBA 7(a) volume (~$432M). Confirm whether it pays Form 159 referral fees. | Fit: Largest hotel SBA 7(a) lender in the US by 2025 volume, so it is a must-call for hotel 7(a) deals. Its 42-state list was not seen, so California lending is unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1791145/000119312526036939/gbfh-ex99_1.htm'),
  ('85f1966a-e182-5bc3-8b16-e0e0363cef99'::uuid, '408c029a-8d52-5e00-a183-2444a849f10e'::uuid, 'Millennium Bank', 'Millennium Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-012: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Multi-state SBA hotel lending (24-25 states per SBA data trackers) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (PLP) | Broker program: No broker program found. Coleman Report named it 2025 SBA Hospitality Lender of the Year and says it has been a leading SBA 7(a) hotel lender for 15 years. Trackers show 245 7(a) loans / $531.1M (FY2020 to 2025). | Fit: An SBA 7(a) hotel specialist, which suits franchised limited-service hotel deals. Ask whether it lends in CA and pays Form 159 referral fees. HQ state (IL) is from a third-party tracker. | Source: https://colemanreport.com/coleman-awards-millennium-bank-as-hospitality-lender-of-the-year'),
  ('dc6243b5-c45a-5a6a-b615-7e8fd3ab8852'::uuid, 'c26232dd-2660-5e12-a78d-65f0704526ee'::uuid, 'Newtek Bank', 'Newtek Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-013: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (PLP), SBA 504 (via affiliate), Conventional business loans | Broker program: Has a referral program for lenders and other referral sources that send loans Newtek can take (per a third-party review). Newtek is a top-2 national SBA 7(a) lender and has had PLP authority since April 2023. Hotel-specific referral terms not found. Confirm the Form 159 fee policy. | Fit: A national top-tier SBA 7(a) lender with a known referral channel. A good fallback for hotel 7(a) deals that CA community banks decline. Hotel focus not documented. | Source: https://ir.newtekone.com/news-releases/news-release-details/newtek-bank-na-receives-sba-preferred-lenders-program-plp-status'),
  ('784b3ec8-413c-5589-b2a1-9f21b34d794e'::uuid, 'bcf601d2-1ef5-5b2f-9d77-78ac3b6018fb'::uuid, 'Open Bank', 'Open Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-014: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: CA-centric Korean-American bank; SBA loans also made out of state (e.g. Texas motel refinance example) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (mostly variable rate), Commercial real estate | Term: SBA loans up to 25 yr | Broker program: No published broker or referral program found. Filings say SBA loans go mainly to small manufacturing, wholesale, retail, hotel/motel and service businesses, and that the bank sells the 75% guaranteed portion. Ask the SBA desk whether it pays Form 159 referral fees. | Fit: An LA SBA 7(a) lender that names hotels/motels as a core SBA segment. Its lending page shows a $2.775M SBA 7(a) refinance of an independent LA County motel. SBA portfolio was $253.7M at 12/31/2024. Broker channel unconfirmed. | Source: https://myopenbank.com/lending'),
  ('da83fb98-4c67-5e6e-b326-0604a023cf98'::uuid, '85fd60e8-4f9b-55c6-9c7b-d5b37bbf1efb'::uuid, 'PCB Bank', 'PCB Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-015: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: LA-based; SBA 7(a) loans funded in 37 states (per PeerSense) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (PLP) | Broker program: No published broker program found. SBA Preferred Lender (PLP). Trackers show 702 7(a) loans / $905.6M (FY2020 to Q1 FY2026); another tracker says 3,007 loans. Best Western franchise borrowers appear in its SBA data. Confirm Form 159 referral-fee policy with the SBA desk. | Fit: A large Korean-American SBA PLP lender in LA with Best Western franchisees among its borrowers. Hotel-specific program not documented in sources found. | Source: https://sbalenderdata.pages.dev/sba-lender/pcb-bank'),
  ('04e8a0a6-9c45-5bc4-b017-44c9e05235de'::uuid, '931c304c-03f1-57a7-8e5f-978cfa6659b2'::uuid, 'United Midwest Savings Bank', 'United Midwest Savings Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-016: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National: says it lends to businesses in all 50 states; recorded mortgages most active in OH, FL, CA (Elementix) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (loans over $150k), Conventional hotel loans, Hospitality financing | Broker program: Has a broker landing page (simplefinancing-dev.umwsb.com/brokers, seen on a dev subdomain). Its hospitality FAQ says it is ''a national bank, not a broker'' and calls itself ''one of the largest SBA lenders in the country with a specialty in hospitality''. Confirm the broker fee policy. | Broker page: https://simplefinancing-dev.umwsb.com/brokers | Contact: Aaron Hodgkins, Hospitality financing (listed on umwsb.com hospitality page; title not captured) | Fit: A national SBA lender focused on hotels, with heavy recorded-mortgage activity in CA and an apparent broker page. A strong fit for hotel 7(a) acquisitions and refinances. | Source: https://umwsb.com/hospitality-financing'),
  ('c008bd87-2150-5d43-b497-f9c83262f1a9'::uuid, '73f33c9a-8180-5bdf-b463-38c9d1ec670e'::uuid, 'US Metro Bank', 'US Metro Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-017: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: CA-chartered; SBA lending also outside CA | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), USDA, Commercial real estate, C&I | Broker program: No published broker program found. GoSBA''s 2025 FOIA ranking puts US Metro #2 nationally for hotel/motel SBA 7(a) volume (~$190M), and the Korea Herald ranked it #10 among Korean-American SBA lenders (FY2026). OCBJ says it specializes in small-business and franchisee loans. Confirm Form 159 referral-fee policy. | Fit: An Orange County Korean-American bank that ranks second nationally for hotel SBA 7(a) volume. A top call for SoCal hotel 7(a) deals. Broker channel not documented. | Source: https://gosbaloans.com/ranking/industry-ranking/all-other-traveler-accommodation-sba-loans/'),
  ('3269266a-1db7-5127-bb48-82c509c0969f'::uuid, 'ba222c62-9ba8-5735-9fca-2564588c94f7'::uuid, 'American Bank, N.A. - Hospitality Lending', 'American Bank, N.A. (Dallas) - Hospitality Lending · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-018: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Dallas-Fort Worth bank; hotel lending area not stated | Programs (as published): Conventional hotel loans, SBA 7(a), SBA 504, Commercial lines of credit | Broker program: None published. | Fit: Small hotelier-owned bank with a dedicated hospitality lending page. Its examples include a $5.3M hotel CRE acquisition and a $3.24M SBA hotel refinance. California lending unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.abdallas.bank/hospitality-lending'),
  ('92014f67-c222-5605-89d0-f49f45ea134d'::uuid, 'b29f66af-6b31-5926-b06f-8a64f5fc1acb'::uuid, 'Golden Bank, N.A.', 'Golden Bank, N.A. · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-019: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Texas and California: branches in Tustin, Alhambra, Rowland Heights, Cupertino, Fremont and Millbrae, plus an Irvine loan production office | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), Commercial real estate | Broker program: None found. | Fit: Houston Asian-American bank with six California branches and an Irvine LPO. SBA data shows 136 SBA 7(a) loans totaling $192.8M from FY2020 to Q1 FY2026 (average $1.4M). Hotel lending and broker acceptance unconfirmed. | Source: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Golden_Bank'),
  ('b4cb7a19-3f7f-50b2-bd4c-30764bb05e28'::uuid, '5a0628b3-22c8-5402-a507-ab9530b9a695'::uuid, 'Herring Bank - Hospitality Lending', 'Herring Bank - Hospitality Lending · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-020: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Says it serves hotel owners across the US; marketing is focused on TX, OK, CO (2025 expansion) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504, Conventional hotel loans, Hotel CMBS, Construction, Refinance, Franchise financing | Broker program: No broker program found. Its hospitality unit has an online preliminary application. | Broker page: https://www.herringbank.com/hospitality-lending/preliminary-application | Fit: A dedicated hotel lending group with SBA, CMBS and construction products. Mostly a Texas, Oklahoma and Colorado lender, so CA reach is unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.herringbank.com/hospitality-lending/preliminary-application'),
  ('6e32362a-5dde-5b24-8865-2e68daa7815f'::uuid, '9deb1420-f553-5747-9ea0-d3d6209de17f'::uuid, 'Hotel.Bank', 'Hotel.Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, 1500000000::bigint, 75.0::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-021: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Not stated | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504, Conventional hotel acquisition/refinance (24-mo I/O product) | Leverage: 75% LTV (conventional) | Rate: From WSJ Prime + 1% (conventional) | Term: Up to 5 yr (conventional); 24-mo interest-only product | Recourse: Personal guarantee required | Speed: Advertises expedited approvals and closings | Broker program: No broker program found. Origination fee is 1% or 1.25% (conventional). | Fit: Possibly another desk of First Bank of the Lake, which is unconfirmed, so verify ownership before adding. It is hotel-only with published conventional terms (up to $15M, 75% LTV) plus SBA 7(a)/504. CA lending and broker channel unconfirmed. | Source: https://hotel.bank'),
  ('19bc0084-684c-5100-afe9-5011fa30ab51'::uuid, '80f78cc3-44e4-59f4-b438-dc3520b06930'::uuid, 'KEB Hana LA Financial / Hana Bank USA', 'KEB Hana LA Financial / Hana Bank USA · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-022: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Los Angeles (lending affiliate); Hana Bank USA plans West Coast growth | Programs (as published): Commercial mortgage loans (CML), Corporate lending, Trade finance; Hana Bank USA profile lists SBA, owner-occupied CRE, multifamily and C&I loans | Broker program: None found. | Fit: Korean bank group''s LA lending arm offering commercial mortgage loans. A KEB Hana entity lent $21M on a Koreatown hotel (May 2020), though the exact entity is unconfirmed. SBA hotel activity and broker acceptance unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.kebhana.com/global/us/us06/us0603/index.jsp'),
  ('6b9b6371-c1b8-5af1-b433-0fa3673b979d'::uuid, '5a908228-9a93-5f1b-9f6e-79c83990340b'::uuid, 'Leader Bank - National SBA', 'Leader Bank - National SBA (Lords of Lending) · SBA 7(a) lender', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['COMMERCIAL']::text[], 25000000::bigint, 500000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory BK-034: tier A, high confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (nationwide SBA 7(a) and 504 team) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504, SBA refinance | Broker program: Sponsored Scotsman Guide content aimed at mortgage brokers says referral partners need no new license and are paid a referral fee when the loan funds. It also runs a free SBA training academy for referral partners. Fee amount not published. Apply at learn.lordsoflending.com. | Broker page: https://learn.lordsoflending.com | Second check: Verified (active 2026: Yes). A March 2026 release confirms the national Lords of Lending SBA team (PLP since 2010); referral partners sign up at learn.lordsoflending.com and are paid on funded loans of $250K-$5M nationw… | Fit: A national 7(a)/504 team added in July 2026 (over $860M of 7(a) originated) that recruits mortgage brokers as referral partners. A good fit for Corin''s owner-user SBA flow, though the fee level is unpublished and the program details come from sponsored conten… | Source: https://www.leaderbank.com/news/leader-bank-continues-expansion-addition-national-sba-team'),
  ('172eb586-178a-539f-8d6f-aafb581a26ed'::uuid, '5a908228-9a93-5f1b-9f6e-79c83990340b'::uuid, 'Leader Bank - National SBA', 'Leader Bank - SBA Referral Partner Program · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], 25000000::bigint, 500000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-023: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) loans | Broker program: Documented referral program aimed at mortgage brokers: pays referral fees on funded SBA loans ($250K-$5M), offers a free SBA training academy, a direct line to its team and a written referral agreement. Fees are disclosed on SBA Form 159. | Broker page: https://learn.lordsoflending.com | Fit: One of the few SBA lenders with a written broker-pay program. Hotel appetite and California lending were not confirmed; SBA lender roles are posted in several markets, including LA. | Source: https://www.scotsmanguide.com/sponsored-content/leader-bank/'),
  ('0fda1128-ab1c-5bc1-b07a-bd27226cef3e'::uuid, '6991d77e-f99f-5ff6-b75f-3969eb2f05a3'::uuid, 'Mission Valley Bank', 'Mission Valley Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-024: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: San Fernando / Santa Clarita Valley CA base; SBA loans in 36 states (per PeerSense) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (Preferred Lender since 2007), SBA real estate purchase and refinance, Equipment, Debt restructuring | Broker program: No published broker program found. Trackers show 286 7(a) loans / $477.4M (FY2020 to 2025). Hotel loans not confirmed. | Fit: An LA-area SBA PLP community bank and a possible smaller 7(a) outlet for CA motel deals. No hotel-specific evidence found, so it is only partly relevant. | Source: https://sbalenderdata.pages.dev/sba-lender/mission-valley-bank'),
  ('bb250fb0-76a2-5f0f-891f-f8a0a338711a'::uuid, '77290082-d129-5da3-930d-ff1d572e9b8d'::uuid, 'Plumas Bank', 'Plumas Bank · SBA 7(a) lender', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory BK-039: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: 19 branches in Northern CA (Butte, Lassen, Nevada, Modoc, Plumas, Placer, Shasta, Sutter, Tehama counties) and NV (Washoe, Carson City); SBA lending in 9 state… | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) (nationwide Preferred Lender, variable and fixed-rate; some fixed-rate loans kept on balance sheet), CRE loans | Broker program: A July 2026 sponsored article says its SBA team mainly does business acquisitions and markets to business brokers. It also takes CRE purchase, equipment, refinance and expansion deals. No mortgage-broker fee terms were found. | Second check: Corrected (active 2026: Yes). A July 2026 article confirms Plumas is an active SBA Preferred Lender in nine states (CA-based, plumasbank.com/sba) with SBA volume into FY2026, but no broker or referral program was found,… | Fit: A nationwide SBA PLP with nearly $1B of 7(a) loans since 2007 and an SBA team that actively markets to brokers. Also does Northern California and Reno CRE. A good SBA outlet for owner-user and acquisition-plus-real-estate deals. | Source: https://comstocksmag.com/sponsored/sba-expertise-ensures-lending-success'),
  ('a4844708-0075-5c67-8896-381de238d89c'::uuid, '77290082-d129-5da3-930d-ff1d572e9b8d'::uuid, 'Plumas Bank', 'Plumas Bank - SBA Lending · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-025: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Northern California and Nevada (Reno HQ; Sacramento SBA / CRE loan office) | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), Commercial real estate | Broker program: No broker program found. | Fit: Northern California SBA lender: SBA data shows 429 SBA 7(a) loans totaling $334.4M from FY2020 to Q1 FY2026 (average about $780K), including two Motel 6 loans. Hotels are a side line; its SBA team focuses on business acquisitions. | Source: https://comstocksmag.com/sponsored/sba-expertise-ensures-lending-success'),
  ('ddb2c042-9ca4-5bd4-b3ed-053e8a28b33c'::uuid, 'e8d02a62-48d0-5b00-b230-ae07ec42d7fa'::uuid, 'T Bank', 'T Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-027: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National SBA team | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504 (PLP) | Broker program: No published broker program found. Its lending page describes a national SBA team (PLP) doing 7(a) and 504. ZoomInfo lists a $7.674M SBA 504 IHG hotel loan. | Phone: (972) 720-9045 | Fit: A Dallas SBA PLP bank with national reach and hotel 504 activity. CA lending and broker channel unconfirmed. The phone number is from ZoomInfo. | Source: https://www.tbank.com/lending/'),
  ('b1db3adf-ae30-54ff-b2ce-558981f475c9'::uuid, '744b0b1f-b074-5a3f-b02c-bc5e36a15cbf'::uuid, 'Woori America Bank', 'Woori America Bank · SBA hotel lender (7(a) / 504)', array['SBA_7A']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-028: tier C, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: SBA loans in 13-18 states; top markets CA, TX, NJ, NY, VA | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a) | Broker program: No published broker program found. GoSBA ranks it #94 nationally in 2025 ($74.2M, 95 loans), with California as its heaviest market. Top franchise concepts are restaurants, and no hotel data was found. | Fit: A Korean-American SBA lender whose largest SBA market is CA. Hotel appetite unconfirmed, so it is a secondary 7(a) outlet. | Source: https://wooriamericabank.com/SBA-Loans'),
  ('8333b69f-e890-5d0a-98d0-a1df6b03f1b4'::uuid, '18efa59a-7a42-5e01-b793-031b8d6f1e7c'::uuid, 'CIM Real Estate Debt Solutions', 'CIM Real Estate Debt Solutions · Hotel bridge / PIP', array['PIP_BRIDGE', 'PRIVATE_BRIDGE', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-029: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (major US markets) | Programs (as published): Hotel bridge whole loans, Construction loans, Mezzanine, Acquisition + renovation | Broker program: No published broker program found. In May 2026 CIM closed $154M of hotel loans: a $63M whole-loan refinance of the 192-room Monterey Beach Hotel (CA), a $56M loan on the Kimpton Monaco Pittsburgh, and $35M for the Sheraton Suites Fort Lauderdale West (acquisition/renovation). It began its hospitality lending push in 2023. | Fit: An LA-based platform making large-balance hotel bridge loans, including a 2026 CA coastal hotel refinance. Best for $30M+ hotel bridge/PIP deals. CIM''s former SBA unit (PMC) was sold to Peachtree, so that is a separate business. HQ is from CIM Group''s public… | Source: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260526392796/en/'),
  ('cf011cbb-c264-54fb-81b1-77cdd65b3e1f'::uuid, '0bec0207-6aa2-564b-8977-a322f7448c11'::uuid, 'Siguler Guff - Credit & Special Situations', 'Siguler Guff - Credit & Special Situations (real estate lending) · Hotel bridge / PIP', array['PIP_BRIDGE', 'PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'MULTIFAMILY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-030: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (deals found in CA and TX) | Programs (as published): Bridge loans, Mezzanine loans | Broker program: No published broker page. Intermediary evidence: in July 2025 its Credit & Special Situations team led a $13.9M bridge loan, announced by Thomas Financial Group, on two historic Sierra foothill hotels (National Exchange Hotel, Nevada City; Holbrooke Hotel, Grass Valley), to be taken out by a $14.3M USDA B&I loan. In Sept 2025 it closed an $11M mezz loan on Waco, TX apartments… | Fit: Private credit lender with a recent California hotel bridge loan under $15M on an intermediary-led deal, used as bridge-to-USDA. Thomas Financial Group (already in the directory) is the proven route in. | Source: https://markets.financialcontent.com/winslow/article/gnwcq-2025-7-29-thomas-financial-group-closes-143-million-usda-loan-in-just-35-days-to-preserve-and-reposition-two-historic-california-boutique-hotels'),
  ('12269909-c5f6-5721-9fb8-8a635d3947a1'::uuid, 'bd59ad34-83f9-56a6-b3b0-1414c63ad8b3'::uuid, 'Thomas Financial Group', 'Thomas Financial Group · Hotel bridge / PIP', array['PIP_BRIDGE', 'PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-031: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (USDA B&I; CA hotel deals 2025) | Programs (as published): Hotel bridge-to-USDA B&I, USDA Business & Industry loans, Hospitality bridge loans | Speed: 35-40 days (per 2025 releases) | Broker program: No published broker program found. 2025 deals include a $13.9M bridge (with Siguler Guff) refinanced by a $14.3M USDA B&I loan for the National Exchange Hotel (Nevada City) and the Holbrooke Hotel (Grass Valley), a $19.975M USDA B&I loan for two historic Mendocino hotels, and three hospitality bridge loans totaling over $34M closed in under 40 days (May 2025). | Fit: An active 2025 lender on CA boutique and rural hotels through bridge-to-USDA structures. It fits non-urban CA hotel acquisitions and renovations that are outside SBA limits. Broker terms unknown. | Source: https://rss.globenewswire.com/news-release/2025/07/29/3123257/0/en/Thomas-Financial-Group-Closes-14-3-Million-USDA-Loan-in-Just-35-Days-to-Preserve-and-Reposition-Two-Historic-California-Boutique-Hotels.html'),
  ('576673a0-2b13-5268-a533-edc7d1bf2af1'::uuid, '5354aa20-6bb1-56c7-b958-2cf299d3b184'::uuid, 'Arena Investors', 'Arena Investors (Real Estate Private Investments) · Hedge fund / private credit', array['PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], 500000000::bigint, 5000000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-051: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (US) and international | Programs (as published): Value-add bridge loans, 1st mortgage bridge, Development / transitional loans | Rate: SOFR + 5% to 8% (value-add bridge, per Arena site) | Broker program: No published broker portal, but Arena''s real estate group ''originates bridge and value add loans'' across property types and posts a transactions page. California loan on its transactions page: $9M 1st mortgage on a retail center in Yucca Valley, CA (May 2022). Recent example: $31.8M 1st mortgage bridge on an Akron, OH retail center (Aug 2024). | Fit: Published $5M-$50M bridge box at SOFR + 5-8%, a direct size match for Corin''s bridge, hospitality and self-storage deals; California lending shown but the latest CA example is from 2022. | Source: https://www.arenaco.com/investments/real-estate-private-investments/'),
  ('0ebcd14f-b06f-583a-a928-de3d88ea4942'::uuid, '5354aa20-6bb1-56c7-b958-2cf299d3b184'::uuid, 'Arena Investors', 'Arena Investors · Hotel bridge / PIP', array['PIP_BRIDGE', 'PRIVATE_BRIDGE']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-032: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Bridge loans, Special situations, Pre-development / land bridge, 1st mortgage | Broker program: No published broker program found. Arena runs a bridge-loan business and describes a niche, complex-situations strategy. Its CA deals include bridge financing for a planned boutique hotel in St. Helena (Napa Valley) that paid off a maturing land loan and funded pre-development, and a $27M 1st mortgage on a California retail plaza (Oct 2023). | Fit: A special-situations bridge lender for hard hotel deals, such as maturing debt, pre-development or entitlement bridges in CA. Not hotel-only. Broker channel and HQ not confirmed in sources found. | Source: https://www.arenaco.com/arenas-deals/hospitality-expansion/'),
  ('50e8cc54-54c7-57ae-9654-d238c7309cc0'::uuid, 'eca021dd-aa07-56f7-95e3-8d77db7283a8'::uuid, 'Driftwood Lending Partners', 'Driftwood Lending Partners · Hotel bridge / PIP', array['PIP_BRIDGE', 'PRIVATE_BRIDGE', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-033: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (deals in TX, FL and other states) | Programs (as published): Hotel mezzanine loans, Preferred equity, Mezz for refinance/recap and ground-up development | Broker program: No published broker program found. Its lending fund gives mezz and pref equity on existing and ground-up hotels, e.g. a $30M mezz in June 2025 behind a Sheraton Dallas refinance and a $12.1M mezz loan. Over $690M of financings by late 2022. Driftwood is also a borrower and developer (e.g. its Mission Valley, San Diego extended-stay construction). | Fit: A hotel-only mezz/pref equity source for gaps in hotel bridge, PIP and construction stacks. CA lending not documented, though Driftwood develops in San Diego. Verify HQ and CA appetite. | Source: https://platform.reverecre.com/company/driftwood.capital'),
  ('b539db3e-aa53-54fe-b943-d11d0c32050c'::uuid, '39b3a893-4fd5-592d-9822-28b4fe0ad72e'::uuid, 'Arriba Capital', 'Arriba Capital · Hotel construction', array['CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, 80.0::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-034: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National (CA, TN, FL and others) | Programs (as published): Hotel ground-up construction, Hotel construction take-out / refinance (non-recourse) | Leverage: 80% LTC (Woodland CA loan) | Term: 3 yr construction | Broker program: No published broker program found. Deals include a $40.5M ground-up construction loan for a Home2 Suites + Courtyard in Woodland, CA (June 2022), a $67M Nashville dual-brand, a $52.5M hotel construction loan, a $35.75M Florida hotel, and The Scoundrel (July 2025). | Fit: A dedicated hotel construction lender with a CA dual-brand loan at 80% LTC, which fits Corin''s hotel construction line. HQ and broker terms not found in the sources. | Source: https://realestatedaily-news.com/arriba-capital-closes-40500000-hotel-construction-loan-for-adjacent-marriot-courtyard-and-hilton-home2-suites-woodland-ca/'),
  ('51778134-513a-5a83-8a5b-20bfd8ff93bd'::uuid, '011c6bd6-20f9-5b9d-b398-6c01a2b0c757'::uuid, 'HALL Structured Finance', 'HALL Structured Finance · Hotel construction', array['CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-035: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Hotel ground-up construction (1st lien), Hotel bridge, Construction for multifamily | Broker program: No published broker program found. Its CA hotel construction loans include the Park James Hotel in Menlo Park ($26M, 2017), the Andaz in Palm Springs ($55M, 2017), Cambria Suites in Napa and Sonoma ($42M), the Aloft in Glendale ($17.6M, 2018), the Hampton Inn in Watsonville ($23M, 2018) and the Hyatt House in Sacramento (2019). Still active in 2025-2026: Dellshire Resort WI ($… | Fit: Has a long record of 1st-lien construction loans on CA select-service and boutique hotels, so it is a core construction call for CA hotel ground-up. The CA hotel deals found are 2017-2019. Confirm current CA hotel appetite and broker terms. | Source: https://prnewswire.com/news-releases/hall-structured-finance-closes-26m-loan-to-finance-the-construction-of-the-park-james-hotel-in-menlo-park-california-300533090.html'),
  ('999b07d4-732d-5f31-882a-6b41442b5cc8'::uuid, '2d35c729-cbb5-5fc7-9e44-a152323dafd2'::uuid, 'Wallis Bank', 'Wallis Bank · Hotel construction', array['CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-036: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: TX-founded (1906); markets include Houston, Dallas, San Antonio, Los Angeles, Atlanta, Phoenix | Programs (as published): SBA 7(a), SBA 504, SBA hotel construction, Conventional acquisition, construction/development, Working capital lines | Broker program: No published broker program found. SBA Preferred Lender ranked in the top 50 nationally. A 2023 ProjectionHub analysis names it the leading SBA hotel construction lender, with 54 hotel construction approvals averaging about $3.07M. Has a Los Angeles market presence. | Fit: An SBA hotel construction specialist with an LA presence. It fits ground-up limited-service hotel 7(a)/504 construction in CA. Ranking data is from 2023, and the broker channel is unconfirmed. | Source: https://www.projectionhub.com/post/how-to-get-an-sba-loan-for-a-hotel'),
  ('756c7687-2794-512d-8cd6-021abfa91736'::uuid, 'fc3cb33c-f017-553a-a43f-29f3ef218499'::uuid, 'First Utah Bank - Hospitality Lending', 'First Utah Bank - Hospitality Lending · Hotel construction', array['CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory HO-037: tier C, medium confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: Utah-based bank; hotel lending area not stated | Programs (as published): Hotel ground-up construction, Acquisition, Expansion, Renovation, Refinance, SBA 504, SBA 7(a), USDA, Equipment financing, Sale-leaseback | Term: 1 to 25 years with balloon payments | Broker program: None published. Its hospitality page presents the bank as a one-stop shop for hotel construction and acquisition loans plus treasury management. | Fit: Bank with a dedicated hotel lending page claiming over $100M of hotel projects funded since 2014 (another section says over $114M). Fits small hotel construction and SBA deals, but its lending area is unconfirmed and likely Mountain West. | Source: https://firstutahbank.com/?p=6766'),
  ('d12aeb84-d416-516b-a41f-23d6e0506eed'::uuid, '6a651bcd-8fe5-5c76-8354-6056375c60af'::uuid, 'PPM America', 'PPM America (Jackson National Life commercial mortgage loans) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['HOSPITALITY', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], 700000000::bigint, 4000000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], 'non_recourse'::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-001: tier A, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Non-recourse fixed-rate permanent commercial mortgage loans | Term: 10-yr term / 30-yr amortization (July 2026 Novato deal) | Recourse: Non-recourse | Broker program: Takes deals from independent intermediaries. In July 2026 Slatt Capital (independent Northern California mortgage banker, originator Jeff Glenn) arranged a $21M non-recourse 10-yr permanent loan from PPM America on a 213-unit Novato, CA apartment property. Trade profile gives a typical $7M-$40M range across office, retail, multifamily, industrial and hotel. | Second check: Verified (active 2026: Yes). In July 2026 Slatt Capital (an outside broker) arranged a $21M PPM America loan on Novato multifamily, and an Aug 2026 release shows PPM growing its CRE origination team with more than $8B o… | Fit: 2026 life company lending in California arranged by an independent mortgage banker, with a $7M-$40M box that fits Corin''s stabilized multifamily and CRE refinances. Hotels are on the property list, which is unusual for a life company. | Source: https://www.connectcre.com/stories/slatt-capital-arranges-life-company-loan-for-novato-multifamily/'),
  ('a17a47d0-871d-5eff-b2df-1d4686bfead8'::uuid, 'cea1fe8e-9c22-507d-bcb2-a9a9ac4f590e'::uuid, 'Symetra Life Insurance Company', 'Symetra Life Insurance Company (Commercial Mortgage Loans) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], 100000000::bigint, 2000000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-002: tier A, high confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National; traded.co lists 14 financed deals (about $219M) in California | Programs (as published): Permanent loans on completed (stabilized) commercial and multifamily properties | Term: 10-yr and 15-yr fixed seen on CA deals | Broker program: Lends through mortgage bankers (correspondents), not brokers, per Symetra''s own page; most loans $1M-$10M, completed properties only. California deals arranged by independent and correspondent intermediaries: $16M Fontana, CA retail refinance with broker Michael Kaplan (President, Slatt Capital); $8M 10-yr fixed refinance of Pointe Red Hill office, Tustin, CA, arranged by Walk… | Broker page: https://financialprofessionals.symetra.com/SymetraMortgage/MortgageBankers/ | Second check: Corrected (active 2026: Yes). Symetra lends only through mortgage-banker correspondents (its Mortgage Bankers page was added), made a Dec 2025 loan, and has a Dec 2023 $16.25M Vista CA loan; no 2025-2026 CA loan was fou… | Fit: The most reachable life company in this set for California small-balance deals: loans of $1M-$20M, repeated CA activity, and California mortgage bankers (Slatt Capital, Walker & Dunlop) that already place loans with it. Corin should submit through or co-broke… | Source: https://financialprofessionals.symetra.com/SymetraMortgage/'),
  ('cac2fbe1-5aaf-5397-a8b8-6e4e28047bb8'::uuid, 'ddd8a84e-eb52-52a6-8fde-9c79f8157da5'::uuid, 'Ameritas Life Insurance Corp.', 'Ameritas Life Insurance Corp. (Commercial Mortgage & Real Estate) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], 100000000::bigint, 1000000000::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-003: tier B, high confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National, MSAs of 250,000+ population within regions served by its core correspondents | Programs (as published): Fixed-rate permanent loans, Short-term bridge loans (office generally excluded) | Leverage: Bridge: 75% of underwritten value | Term: Permanent: 10-25 yr terms, up to 30 yr amortization; Bridge: 3 yr + two 1-yr extensions | Broker program: Correspondent model: Ameritas says its program connects borrowers with mortgage banking firms and loan originators nationwide, and it lends in markets served by its core correspondents. Analyst job postings describe calling on mortgage banking correspondents. Larger loans considered. Also takes intermediary-arranged deals: JLL arranged a 5-yr fixed-rate Ameritas acquisition lo… | Broker page: https://www.ameritas.com/industry-professionals/commercial-real-estate/ | Fit: Small-balance life company ($1M-$10M) that also offers bridge loans, a useful fit for Corin''s smaller deals. Access is through Ameritas correspondents, and whether it lends in California depends on correspondent coverage, so confirm. | Source: https://www.ameritas.com/investments/commercial-mortgage-real-estate'),
  ('b303618c-8ed9-50eb-955b-4d0234cc8f01'::uuid, 'e869c260-f5d7-54d3-8020-96dd2035337b'::uuid, 'Barings Real Estate Debt', 'Barings Real Estate Debt (MassMutual commercial mortgage loans) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], array['SENIOR_LIVING', 'HOSPITALITY', 'MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL', 'CONSTRUCTION']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-004: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Fixed-rate permanent loans, Forward permanent loan commitments, Floating-rate / transitional loans | Other source: Construction loans, Bridge / transitional senior loans, Permanent loans; frequent construction pairing with C-PACE (Counterpointe) | Term: 5-yr term on a 2024 Tempe extended-stay hotel loan | Broker program: Not documented in search results. Barings press releases show California and Western lending: $78M on The Townsend (277 units, Mission Valley, San Diego, about 2024), $24M on an extended-stay hotel in Tempe, AZ, $114M on a Reno, NV industrial property, and a $133.4M forward permanent commitment (22 Fulton, 2026). | Other source: No published broker program. Large-balance balan… | Fit: MassMutual''s real estate lender, active in San Diego multifamily and willing to lend on hotels. Typical loans are $20M+. How it sources loans is unconfirmed. Also fits: Mortgage REIT / large-balance debt fund. | Source: https://www.barings.com/en-us/guest/contact/media/news/barings-provides-78-million-financing-on-the-townsend-in-san-diego-ca'),
