  ('a7b23c12-ad28-5152-bdac-16d58d5d70e1'::uuid, '74d017b5-ac08-5532-b8f6-1600e4e6324d'::uuid, 'National Life Group', 'National Life Group (commercial mortgage loans) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-008: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Permanent commercial mortgage loans | Broker program: Not documented. Top deals on its traded.co profile include a $26.75M multifamily loan in San Diego, CA and a $15.9M warehouse loan in Long Beach, CA (about $80M across tracked deals). | Fit: Mid-size life company with recent Southern California multifamily and industrial loans of $15M-$27M. How it sources loans (direct or through correspondents) is unconfirmed. | Source: https://traded.co/company/national-life-group/'),
  ('c3d05e8b-096c-5e20-864f-3c7d8c4c3b58'::uuid, '973420b0-2147-5591-9a32-e8147095b575'::uuid, 'Northwestern Mutual Real Estate', 'Northwestern Mutual Real Estate (commercial mortgage loans) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-009: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Fixed-rate permanent first mortgages (large-balance) | Broker program: Not documented on a lender page in this round. traded.co lists about 40 closed California deals (about $6B of tracked volume; largest California loan $869M tied to a La Habra property), most recent dated Oct 14, 2025. Tracked deals are commonly placed by large intermediaries (JLL, CBRE). | Fit: One of the most active life company lenders in California by deal count, but large-balance and reached mostly through national intermediaries. A small broker would likely co-broker with a large mortgage banker. | Source: https://traded.co/company/northwestern-mutual-/'),
  ('d5b97240-6be0-5c54-9f6c-6bab098f9dfd'::uuid, '12d746df-95a6-53b7-b8f8-1e3a27be283b'::uuid, 'Pacific Life Insurance Company', 'Pacific Life Insurance Company (Real Estate Investments / commercial mortgage loans) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-010: tier B, low confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Long-term fixed-rate permanent loans (including on assets still in lease-up), Commercial mortgage loans (balance sheet) | Broker program: No published broker program. Takes intermediary-arranged deals: JLL Capital Markets arranged a $345M long-term fixed-rate Pacific Life refinance of Miro (630 units, downtown San Jose) while the property was still in lease-up (2022). FY2025 statutory filings show about $17.7B of commercial mortgage loans. The largest single loan at the Pacific Life & Annuity affiliate was $33M. | Fit: California-headquartered life company that lends in the state and will fund assets still in lease-up. Placements seen are through large intermediaries and its small-loan appetite is unconfirmed, so call the real estate investments group. | Source: https://commercialobserver.com/2022/07/pacific-life-refis-multifamily-high-rise-in-california-with-345m-loan/'),
  ('3d9de960-bd39-51d9-89d0-b4fadc86ad54'::uuid, 'f6dd3b75-b4e2-5c83-b0eb-14b8f54063b0'::uuid, 'Principal Real Estate', 'Principal Real Estate (Principal Life commercial & multifamily mortgage loans) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-011: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Core commercial & multifamily first-lien private mortgage loans (life company balance sheet and institutional accounts) | Broker program: Not documented in search results. Principal''s own CML page says deal sizes run from under $10M to over $100M per transaction, on first liens against well-leased income-producing properties. No correspondent list found. California activity: Principal Life provided a $42M loan on a Culver City mixed-use property (2021, per traded.co). | Fit: Large life company lender for stabilized core assets. The way it sources loans (direct or through correspondents) was not confirmed, so a small broker would likely reach it through a mortgage banker correspondent. | Source: https://www.principalam.com/us/insights/real-estate/commercial-multifamily-mortgage-loan-cml-investments'),
  ('2e4aca62-8d39-5457-9e5c-d2f19551033d'::uuid, '3238b462-743c-57de-a403-910c72fc8e5e'::uuid, 'Protective Life Insurance Company', 'Protective Life Insurance Company (Commercial Mortgages) · Life insurance company', array['BANK_LIFE_CO']::text[], array['MULTIFAMILY', 'COMMERCIAL']::text[], 300000000::bigint, 5000000000::bigint, 75.0::numeric, null::numeric, array['first']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory IN-012: tier B, high confidence, lends in CA: Unconfirmed. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: National | Programs (as published): Fixed-rate permanent commercial mortgages | Leverage: 75% LTV; min 1.20x DSCR | Broker program: The commercial mortgage page has an ''Approved firms'' section and says Protective works with a variety of firms across different categories, i.e. an approved list of mortgage banker / broker firms. Deploys roughly $1.5B a year in CRE debt. | Broker page: https://www.protective.com/additional-services/commercial-mortgages/approved-firms | Fit: Published, broker-friendly box ($3M-$50M, 75% LTV, 1.20x DSCR) and an approved-firm program. A small broker should ask to be added to the approved list or co-broker with a listed firm. California activity not confirmed in search results. | Source: https://www.protective.com/commercial-mortgages/'),
