  ('08eef57f-c785-5a06-a6fc-980bf61bd687'::uuid, '84df28e3-83f1-542a-82ae-90a4801350d4'::uuid, 'AmPac Business Capital', 'AmPac Business Capital · SBA 504 CDC', array['SBA_7A', 'SBA_504']::text[], array['COMMERCIAL']::text[], null::bigint, null::bigint, null::numeric, null::numeric, array['first', 'second']::text[], null::text, null::numeric, null::numeric, 'Directory BK-028: tier B, medium confidence, lends in CA: Yes. States not set (empty means nationwide): confirm the footprint before approving. | Footprint: California, Arizona, Nevada | Programs (as published): SBA 504, SBA 7(a) | Broker program: Its 504 sales manager spoke at Coleman Report''s ''SBA Loan Broker & Lender Table'' (July 2024), so it actively works with brokers. Its compliance statement says it does not pay referral fees that would violate SBA SOP 50 10 or RESPA. No written broker program found. | Phone: 909-915-1706 | Email: info@ampac.com | Fit: An Inland Empire 504 CDC (51 504 loans in 2024) covering CA, AZ and NV that also offers 7(a). Broker-friendly in practice, but Corin''s fee must come from the borrower or the bank. | Source: https://www.sba.gov/funding-programs/loans/504-loans/list-certified-development-companies'),
